49d8d697-e4fb-4106-9aae-fb4398433e4a|Guinea-Bissau: Stafff Report for the 2025 Article IV Consultation, Eighth Review Under the Extended Credit Fac|75|text|16. Guinea-Bissau is assessed to have weak debt carrying capacity, unchanged from the previous DSA. The Composite Indicator (CI) score for Guinea-Bissau is 2.65 based on data from the October 2024 WEO and the 2023 Country Policy and Institutional Assessment (CPIA) of the World Bank (Text Table 6). This score is below the 2.69 cutoff, resulting in a weak debt-carrying capacity.
