e80f2003-c7dc-4862-90ce-7b4ad74f8244|Grenada: Staff Report for the 2019 Article IV Consultation—Debt Sustainability Analysis|40|text|10. Grenada continues to be assessed at medium debt-carrying capacity.The rating is based on the CI score, which captures the impact of the different factors through a weighted sum of the 2017 World Bank's Country Policy and Institutional Assessment (CPIA) score,the country's real GDP growth remittances, international reserves,and world growth. $^{7}$ Under the CPIA,Grenada continues to be rated as a medium performer,with the average rating of 3.48 for 2015-17.
