bb71224b-fd58-4ab9-a583-7040d2df2ec5|Republic of Uzbekistan: 2021 Article IV Consultation—Press Release; and Staff Report|55|text|Uzbekistan's Composite Indicator (CI) score is 3.16. $^{3}$ The strong CI score reflects high average international reserves (about 60 percent of the 10-year average of imports) and high average Country Policy and Institutional Assessment (CPIA) ratings. It represents a modest decline from Uzbekistan's CI score of 3.21 at the time of the May 2020 DSA. The decline was primarily caused by lower projected global growth due to the more prolonged impact of the COVID
