bf1954ec-97a3-4b09-acfe-0d73badffedb|Zambia: Staff Report for the 2023 Article IV Consultation, First Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arr|75|text|21. Zambia's debt-carrying capacity under the Composite Indicator (CI) rating is assessed as weak, unchanged from the previous DSA. $^{14}$ The latest CI score of 2.59 remains below the cut-off for medium debt-carrying capacity of 2.69, $^{15}$ so the assessment of debt sustainability is based on the thresholds for a weak debt-carrying capacity country.
