f2758dcb-8ac2-4890-a819-baa59c84a8c3|Maldives: Staff Report for the 2022 Article IV Consultation—Debt Sustainability Analysis|68|text|10. The debt carrying capacity of the Maldives remains weak.The composite indicator (CI) score is 2.40 (less than the 2.69 threshold) using the April 2022 WEO and the 2022 World Bank Country Policy and Institutional Assessment (CPIA). The CI is based on a weighted average of several factors such as the country's real GDP growth, remittances, international reserves, world growth, and the CPIA score. The calculation of the CI is based on 10-year averages of the variables, across five years of historical data and five years of projections, and the corresponding CPIA.
