1a1d5b64-bbb2-4245-afbe-f7fcd67382a5|United Republic of Tanzania: Staff Report for the 2025 Article IV Consultation, Fifth Review Under the Extende|59|text|10. The country's debt-carrying capacity applied to this DSA is categorized as medium, same as in the previous DSA. The calculated Composite Indicator (CI) Index is 2.88 (text table 5), down from 2.89 in the June 2024 DSA (Text Table 6), based on the October 2024 WEO and the 2023 CPIA data. The corresponding indicative thresholds are: (i) 40 percent for the present value (PV) of external debt-to-GDP ratio; (ii) 180 percent for the PV of external debt-to-exports ratio; (iii) 15 percent for the external debt service-to-exports ratio; and (iv) 18 percent for the external debt service-to-revenue ratio. The benchmark of the PV of total public debt for medium debt-carrying capacity is 55 percent.
